Licensed under the MIT license; see LICENSE. dtoa.c contains additional
upstream copyright and license notices.

The Linux C11 configuration headers are supplied here. load.c is patched to
abort lexical scanning when a token buffer allocation fails. This prevents
truncated tokens from being accepted or read beyond the token buffer. Bounded
error-message copies in load.c and error.c avoid GCC truncation warnings.
Trailing whitespace in upstream lookup3.h comments is normalized.
See c-core/tests/jansson_alloc_failure_test.c.
